  "question": {
    "text": "The side $A B$ of $\\triangle A B C$ is fixed and is of length $2 a$ unit. The vertex moves in the plane such that the vertical angle is always constant and is $\\alpha$. Let $x$-axis be along $A B$ and the origin be at $A$. Then the locus of the vertex is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$x^2+y^2+2 a x \\sin \\alpha+a^2 \\cos \\alpha=0$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$x^2+y^2-2 a x-2 a y \\cot \\alpha=0$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$x^2+y^2-2 a x \\cos \\alpha-a^2=0$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$x^2+y^2-a x \\sin \\alpha-$ ay $\\cos \\alpha=0$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let, $c=z=x+i y$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n&\\arg \\left(\\frac{2 \\mathrm{a}-\\mathrm{z}}{0-\\mathrm{z}}\\right)=\\alpha \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow \\arg \\left(\\frac{(\\mathrm{x}-2 \\mathrm{a})+\\mathrm{iy}}{\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{iy}}\\right)=\\alpha \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x}^2+\\mathrm{y}^2-2 \\mathrm{ax}-2 \\mathrm{ay} \\cot \\alpha=0\n\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"assets\\st0009_cbf0342aca07.png\">"
  }
